    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 test green).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe response DTO (`OwnerDto`) is generated from `openapi.yml`, and derived read-only fields are computed in the MapStruct `OwnerMapper` via util classes (the existing pattern for `initials`, `membershipLevel`, `identityKey`, etc.). I followed that same pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` field (integer 0\u20139) to the Owner schema, right after `customerCode`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/CheckDigits.java`** (new) \u2014 computes the Luhn check digit over the decimal digits of `customerCode`, ignoring non-digit characters like the `-` separators. The algorithm matches the test's `luhn()` exactly: right-to-left, doubling every second digit starting with the rightmost, casting out nines, returning `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `checkDigit` calling `CheckDigits.checkDigitFor(owner)`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode`, which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact `checkDigit`, passes.\n\nNote: this is a computed value derived from `customerCode` at response time \u2014 it isn't persisted on the `Owner` entity, consistent with the other derived DTO fields.",
